n":"Cabinet Office","detail":"In February 2012 she was chief of staff to the Cabinet Office minister Francis Maude.","source":{"title":"Can David Cameron be made to understand what women want?, The Guardian, 15 February 2012","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2012/feb/15/women-equality"}},{"phase":"career","start":"2012","end":"2015","title":"Political adviser, head of family and education policy","organisation":"Number 10 Policy Unit","detail":"She served in the No 10 policy unit under David Cameron from 2012 to 2015.","source":{"title":"Laura Trott MP profile, politics.co.uk","url":"https://www.politics.co.uk/people/laura-trott/"}},{"phase":"career","start":null,"end":"2016-07","title":"Director of strategic communications","organisation":"10 Downing Street","detail":"She was director of strategic communications at No 10 for David Cameron until July 2016.","source":{"title":"General Election 2019: Conservative Laura Trott looks safe in Sevenoaks, Kent Online, 17 November 2019","url":"https://www.kentonline.co.uk/sevenoaks/news/general-election-2019-we-can-deliver-what-sevenoaks-needs-says-laura-trott-216653/"}},{"phase":"career","start":"2017-09","end":null,"title":"Partner","organisation":"Portland Communications","detail":"She became a partner at Portland Communications in September 2017.","source":{"title":"Wikipedia: Laura Trott (politician)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Trott_(politician)"}},{"phase":"politics","start":null,"end":null,"title":"Joined the Conservative Party","organisation":"Conservative Party","detail":"She says she has been in the Conservatives since she was a teenager.","source":{"title":"Rising stars: Meet the Conservative Party's ambitious young MPs, PoliticsHome, 3 October 2023","url":"https://www.politicshome.com/thehouse/article/rising-stars-meet-conservative-partys-ambitious-young-mps"}},{"phase":"politics","start":"2010-05","end":"2010-05","title":"Elected councillor, Frognal and Fitzjohns ward","organisation":