tor","detail":"Worked for a firm of solicitors that provided legal services to trade union members and specialised in industrial injury cases.","source":{"url":"https://www.politics.co.uk/people/douglas-alexander/","title":"politics.co.uk: Douglas Alexander"},"organisation":null},{"end":"1982","phase":"politics","start":"1982","title":"Joined the Labour Party","detail":"Joined the Labour Party as a schoolboy.","source":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_Alexander","title":"Wikipedia: Douglas Alexander"},"organisation":"Labour Party"},{"end":"1995","phase":"politics","start":"1995","title":"Selected as Labour candidate for Perth and Kinross byelection","detail":"Selected to stand for Westminster for the first time, in the Perth and Kinross byelection.","source":{"url":"https://www.holyrood.com/news/view,trading-places-back-in-government-douglas-alexander-is-a-new-man","title":"Holyrood: Trading places: back in government, Douglas Alexander is a new man"},"organisation":"Labour Party"},{"end":"1995-05","phase":"politics","start":"1995-05","title":"Labour candidate, Perth and Kinross byelection","detail":"Stood for Labour in the Perth and Kinross byelection, which was won by the SNP.","source":{"url":"https://members-api.parliament.uk/api/Members/632/Biography","title":"UK Parliament Members API: Douglas Alexander biography"},"organisation":"Labour Party"},{"end":"1997-05","phase":"politics","start":"1997-05","title":"Labour candidate for Perth","detail":"Stood for Labour in Perth at the 1997 general election and came third with 11,036 votes.","source":{"url":"https://api.parliament.uk/uk-general-elections/elections/23585","title":"UK Parliament: 1997 General Election, Perth"},"organisation":"Labour Party"},{"end":"1997-11","phase":"politics","start":"1997-11","title":"Labour candidate, Paisley South","detail":"Elected at the Paisley South byelection on 6 November 1997.","source":{"url":"https://membersafter1832.historyofparliamentonline.org/members/60","tit